{"ardent":{"id":"5708bbbe-5ee1-4840-92fe-a12a97adadd7","word":"ardent","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"full of ardour","word":"ardente"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"This ardent exploration, absorbing all his energy and interest, made him forget for the moment the mystery of his heritage and the anomaly that cut him off from all his fellows.","ref":"1956, Arthur C. Clarke, The City and the Stars, page 43:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[5,11]],"id":"a477f08a-16f0-4058-874e-30440f3e5369"},{"text":"I see by your eagerness and the wonder and hope which your eyes express, my friend, that you expect to be informed of the secret with which I am acquainted; that cannot be; listen patiently until the end of my story, and you will easily perceive why I am reserved upon that subject. I will not lead you on, unguarded and ardent as I then was, to your destruction and infallible misery.","ref":"1818, Mary Shelley, chapter 4, in Frankenstein, archived from the original on 30 Oct 2011:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[321,327]],"id":"ce1f3da8-9728-4cfc-9495-a39b78c5de58"},{"text":"Nor gushing tears, nor ardent prayers, shall shake our firm decree.","ref":"1750, “Theodora”, Thomas Morell (lyrics), George Frideric Handel (music):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,29]],"id":"647f1437-c0f3-4877-9d5f-81e3d8607049"}],"links":[["Full","full"],["ardor","ardor"],["expressing","expressing"],["passion","passion"],["spirit","spirit"],["enthusiasm","enthusiasm"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"burning"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["Full of ardor; expressing passion, spirit, or enthusiasm."],"id":"978597de-0fc7-461d-88fc-2b9f11b13086"},{"categories":["English literary terms"],"links":[["Providing","providing"],["light","light"],["heat","heat"]],"raw_glosses":["(literary) Providing light or heat."],"glosses":["Providing light or heat."],"tags":["literary"],"id":"8e2bca90-3843-4160-9dbf-33f73b525447"}],"related":[{"word":"ardency"},{"word":"ardently"},{"word":"ardent spirits"},{"word":"ardor"}],"synonyms":[]},"arduous":{"id":"cd65b3ed-12a9-43bf-ac56-09eadbe847fb","word":"arduous","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"needing or using up much energy","word":"árduo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"hard to climb or traverse","word":"árduo"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The movement towards a peaceful settlement has been a long and arduous political struggle.","bold_text_offsets":[[63,70]],"type":"example","id":"12e4f880-3a3b-4402-9f0b-d7532e1f421c"},{"text":"Chelsea survived and can now turn their attentions to the Champions League final against Bayern Munich in Germany later this month as they face an increasingly arduous task to finish in the Premier League's top four.","ref":"2012 May 5, Phil McNulty, “Chelsea 2-1 Liverpool”, in BBC Sport:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[160,167]],"id":"04c45c3c-bfcf-4459-91e6-89073e7cfc56"}],"links":[["energy","energy"],["endurance","endurance"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["Needing or using up much energy; testing powers of endurance."],"id":"6aa30acd-d13e-4eef-b000-d5264009455e"},{"examples":[{"text":"1805-1814, Dante, Henry Francis Cary (translator), The Divine Comedy\nWhere flames the arduous Spirit of Isidore.","type":"quotation","id":"a30dc50f-9dd3-4a7a-ac19-1be7c3788fe2"}],"categories":["English terms with obsolete senses","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["burning","burning"],["ardent","ardent"]],"raw_glosses":["(obsolete) burning; ardent"],"glosses":["burning; ardent"],"tags":["obsolete"],"id":"979fa853-4076-4271-b516-fda76ba8f9b8"},{"examples":[{"text":"Beyond the river, an arduous slope rises 3286 feet in 13 miles.","ref":"1974, Sue Bowder, The American biking atlas & touring guide, page 77:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[21,28]],"id":"f41b9a1b-3538-4cbd-b979-51e59ec5be0e"},{"text":"Mike looked up from the arduous mountain trail. They'd been climbing for five hours and he was beginning to feel irritable.","ref":"1999, Scott Ciencin, Mike Fredericks, Dinoverse:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[24,31]],"id":"a54c3f3a-d88c-40ff-9e3a-9d59a860b198"},{"text":"Survivor reaches as many as 28 million viewers who watch contestants win a new Pontiac or guzzle Mountain Dew after scaling an arduous cliff.","ref":"2006, Jack W. Plunkett, Plunkett's Entertainment & Media Industry Almanac 2006:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[127,134]],"id":"8acc68e0-d48b-4300-a73b-85471c27b69c"}],"links":[["Difficult","difficult"],["exhausting","exhausting"],["traverse","traverse"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["Difficult or exhausting to traverse."],"id":"e7ac7bbd-e0e8-403a-9df5-52ef8939a18e"}],"related":[{"word":"arduity"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"burdensome"},{"word":"demanding"},{"word":"exhausting"},{"word":"fatiguing"},{"word":"laborious"},{"word":"onerous"},{"word":"strenuous"},{"word":"strugglesome"},{"word":"wearisome"},{"word":"uphill"}]},"arduously":{"id":"87e576de-770e-4834-90aa-ff882840e24c","word":"arduously","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"in an arduous manner","word":"arduamente"}],"pos":"adv","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["arduous","arduous"]],"glosses":["in an arduous manner"],"categories":["English adverbs","English entries with etymology texts","English entries with etymology trees","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms derived from the Proto-Indo-European root *leyg- (like)","English terms suffixed with -ly (adverbial)","Entries with translation boxes","Pages using etymon with no ID","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Pages with etymology trees","Terms with Persian translations","Terms wi